roofline-gap
============

How far a real LLM decode step is from its roofline, and where the gap goes.

Setup: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, bf16, vLLM 0.32.0, CUDA graphs on, one
A100-SXM4-40GB with the SM clock locked at 1215 MHz. 53 (batch b, prompt
length s) points, b = 1..256, s = 128..8192, 64 output tokens; only pure
decode steps are timed.


Results
-------

- The measured step is 1.25-1.72x the datasheet roofline (312 TFLOP/s,
  1555 GB/s).
- Roofline-style tools underpredict it by 20-49% (hand roofline, LLM-Viewer,
  GenZ, aiconfigurator SOL); aiconfigurator EMPIRICAL/SILICON by 9-27%.
- The gap, one term at a time (analysis/ladder.py):
    R0  roofline at datasheet ceilings
    R1  + measured ceilings (1449 GB/s HBM read, 253 TFLOP/s GEMM)
    R2  + measured GEMM time at M = b (the largest term for b >= 32)
    R3  + measured vLLM FA2 attention kernel
  R3 is within 0.7 ms of the measured step; the rest is small kernels and
  GPU idle time.


Reproduce the numbers (CPU only, from results/)
-----------------------------------------------

    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python analysis/ladder.py


Re-run the experiments (A100, root for clock locking, Nsight Systems)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

    exp/setup.sh       # vLLM + model weights into models/llama31-8b
    exp/run_all.sh     # E1-E4, raw results into results/

  E1  GEMM and HBM microbenchmarks          results/e1_gemm.json
  E2  per-step decode time over the grid    results/e2_steps.jsonl
  E3  per-kernel breakdown (nsys)           results/e3_*.jsonl
  E4  decode attention microbenchmark       results/e4_*.json

SM_CLOCK=none runs without clock locking.

Baseline predictions (results/baselines.csv): install
requirements-baselines.txt (Python 3.12), clone LLM-Viewer into
third_party/LLM-Viewer (or set LLMVIEWER_DIR), then run
python analysis/baselines.py.


